Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I'm able to color the tips (although the color order is incorrect, so please check.)

library(ggtree)
set.seed(123)
tree <- rtree(10)

#Colored tips
data <- data.frame(taxa=c("t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t10"),place=c(rep("red",5),rep("blue",5)))
p <- ggtree(tree)
p <- p %<+% data + geom_tippoint(aes(color=place)) + geom_tiplab()
p #Note that the colors are inverted. t1 to t5 should be blue, not red, and the contrary for t6 to t10. Is this a bug?

And color OTUS

#Colored OTUS
cls <- list(c1=c("t1", "t2","t8","t7"),
            c2=c("t3", "t4", "t10"),
            c3=c( "t9","t6","t5"))
tree1 <- groupOTU(tree, cls)
p1 <- ggtree(tree1, aes(color=group)) +
        scale_color_manual(values=c("black", "red","green","blue"))

But I'm unable to combine them?

#Combined?
p2 <- p1 %<+% data + geom_tippoint(aes(color=place))
p2
Error: Insufficient values in manual scale. 6 needed but only 4 provided.

How can I create plots in which the edges have certain color and the tip a different one? Why is the order of the colors in p inverted?

From u2dfd8918c2aa0162 at groups.google.com  Wed Feb  1 19:29:41 2017
From: u2dfd8918c2aa0162 at groups.google.com (Ryan Kepler)
